{"skill":{"slug":"zero-trust","displayName":"Zero Trust"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770042199717,"changelog":"**Initial release: Establishes security-first protocols for all high-risk operations.**\n\n- Introduces zero-trust guidelines for agent operations involving external resources, installations, or credentials.\n- Requires explicit human approval for sensitive actions such as sending emails, installing packages, or clicking unknown links.\n- Outlines STOP → THINK → VERIFY → ASK → ACT → LOG flow for all external actions.\n- Defines strict credentials handling: never log or expose, always store securely.\n- Provides clear red flags to identify risky operations and immediate STOP criteria.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3012,"sha256":"46238c45b71b0948a1c45e99b8f391b44e3b44bb9a16ef4e42318061425fdcef","contentType":null},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1934,"sha256":"acff1f507c3b9ce4d9a18f440f0a44a5f1b638977eb3c0c08ace6b8ee64dad64","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789028565944,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"2adfc899d604f53d4eea4f1ec03dab1fce9641a2e1892a50f41ffe3097557266","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/2adfc899d604f53d4eea4f1ec03dab1fce9641a2e1892a50f41ffe3097557266","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: zero-trust\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThis skill bundle is designed to implement a 'Zero Trust Security Protocol' for the OpenClaw agent. The `SKILL.md` file contains extensive instructions for the agent to exercise extreme caution, verify sources, seek human approval for risky actions (e.g., installations, external API calls, URL clicks, credential handling), and identify common red flags (e.g., `sudo` requests, obfuscated code, urgency pressure, typosquatting). All instructions are defensive in nature, aiming to prevent data exfiltration, unauthorized execution, and other malicious activities, rather than performing them. There is no evidence of prompt injection with malicious intent, nor any other high-risk behaviors.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160897757},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":48,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":4,"checkedAt":1789028565944},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a security-guidance skill with no executable payload, but its authorization rules are broad and under-defined enough that users should review it before installing.","dimensions":[{"detail":"For a security skill, treating unrestricted local file operations as safe to do freely is overbroad because local reads, writes, deletes, and permission changes can affect sensitive data and project integrity.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The inspected artifact is a single Markdown SKILL.md file with no executable scripts, dependencies, installer, or package metadata beyond the skill text.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The trigger covers nearly all external-resource and irreversible-effect workflows, while the instructions do not define how Pat is authenticated or how these rules relate to the current user, platform policy, or higher-priority controls.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill does not install persistence mechanisms or request elevated privileges, though it does instruct agents to store credentials under ~/.config with mode 600 when credentials are handled.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated zero-trust purpose is coherent, but the skill makes an undefined named person, Pat, the approval authority and also permits all local file operations without approval, which conflicts with its caution-first framing.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review and narrow this skill before installing: replace Pat with the authenticated user or configured administrator, state that platform and system policies take precedence, and limit no-approval local file activity to non-sensitive read-only workspace operations. There is no evidence of malicious code or exfiltration in the inspected artifact.","findings":"[RA1] expected: The cited text is a red-flag checklist item warning about requests to disable security features; I found no artifact-backed self-modification, code modification, or runtime payload.\n[SQP-1] expected: Broad activation is consistent with a zero-trust guidance skill, but its breadth increases the impact of the under-defined approval authority.\n[EA2] unexpected: The DO FREELY section explicitly includes local file operations without approval, which is too broad for destructive or sensitive filesystem actions.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The artifact does not distinguish read-only workspace access from sensitive reads, writes, deletes, moves, or permission changes.\n[T01] unexpected: The hard-coded approval authority Pat is present in the artifact and lacks authentication, scope, or precedence language.\n[T09] unexpected: The unrestricted local-file exemption is present and materially under-scoped for a security-oriented policy skill.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789028565944}}}}}